title: Combatting Climate Change
new-page: true
is-card: true
on-arrival: climate_policy_timer += 5; month_actions += 1
view-if: dems_in_government = 1
card-image: img/portraits/BaadeFritz.jpg
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet

= Climate Policy

Through both executive departments, and hopefully congress, we can push the country to reduce its pollutions and use of dirty energy, and towards the use of green energy.

- @strengthen_pollution_regulations
- @cancel_oil_drilling
- @carbon_tax
- @declare_a_climate_emergy
- @root: Do not enact any policies for now.
- @easy_discard
- @cancel_advisor_action

@strengthen_pollution_regulations
title: Strengthen Pollution Regulations
subtitle: The EPA will set stricter federal pollution standards on power generation and vehicles. This will anger coal country, especially since we have not provided any aid for job transitioning.
unavailable-subtitle: [? if democrat_supreme_court_seats < republican_supreme_court_seats : The <span style="color: #DE0100;">**Conservative**</span> majority on the supreme court will strike down any further expansion. ?]
choose-if: times_strengthened_pollution <= 2 and democrat_supreme_court_seats < republican_supreme_court_seats or democrat_supreme_court_seats > republican_supreme_court_seats
on-arrival: times_strengthened_pollution += 1; republican_radicalization +=1; green_backlash +=1; climate_progress +=3; blue_dog_dissent +=2
max-visits: 4

The EPA announces a series of new regulations hitting vehicle tailpipes and dirty powerplants. This necessary step will improve the longterm health of the enviornment. Republicans will try and blame job losses in coal states on these measures. [? if manchin_is_a_dem = 1 : Joe Manchin makes his disagreements with this policy clear. ?]


@cancel_oil_drilling
title: Revoke Visa's For Projects Involving Dirty Energy, And Speed Up Approval For Green Energy Projects
subtitle: This is more effective in aiding the transition to green energy then strengthening pollution regulations, but may lead to more backlash. 
on-arrival: republican_radicalization +=2; green_backlash +=2; climate_progress +=6; inflation +=0.1; blue_dog_dissent +=4; economic_growth -=0.1; Q.state_buffs.PA = (Q.state_buffs.PA || 0) + 4; window.simulate_polling();

max-visits: 3

A series of dirty energy projects, especially in alaska and the pacific are canceled. This pleases those with enviornmental concerns and will certainly encourage energy companies to switch to green energy production instead, although Republicans will attempt to tie these measures to the cost of living. [? if manchin_is_a_dem = 1 : Joe Manchin makes his disagreements with this policy clear. ?]

@carbon_tax
title: Can We Tax Carbon?
subtitle: +2 budget. This will modestly speed up the transition to green energy. This will harm the economy of states with large gas and coal industries.
choose-if: filibuster_gone = 1
unavailable-subtitle: This will never survive the fillibuster.
on-arrival: budget += 2; republican_radicalization +=5; green_backlash +=5; climate_progress +=15; blue_dog_dissent +=10; economic_growth -=0.2; inflation +=0.25;

WIP 

@declare_a_climate_emergy
title: Declare A National Climate Emergency
subtitle: This allow the limited redirecting of military spending for the construction of green energy projects instead. 
unavailable-subtitle: This allow the limited redirecting of military spending for the construction of green energy projects instead. The <span style="color: #DE0100;">**Conservative**</span> majority on the supreme court would declare this improper.
choose-if: democrat_supreme_court_seats > republican_supreme_court_seats
on-arrival: republican_radicalization +=2; climate_progress +=6; blue_dog_dissent +=3; economic_growth +=0.1; inflation -=0.15
max-visits: 1

Bernie Sanders announces a climate emergency on prime tv. We have unlocked significantly more funding for green energy products, which may help lower general energy prices. Republicans claim this is a fragrant abuse of executive power.